// The gauntlet harness twins' shared library. Metrics.jet names the
// loss-owner category of each metric, Tree.jet reads JSON values by path,
// Axis.jet holds what the axis adapters share (where one runs, the
// publication it reports and its contract rules), CompileThroughput.jet is
// the twin of
// Tools/gauntlet/harness/compile-throughput.mjs (the compile_throughput axis
// contract and adapter), BuildSystem.jet that of the contract and adapter
// exports of Tools/gauntlet/harness/build-system.mjs, Coverage.jet the
// census library of Tools/gauntlet/harness/coverage.mjs,
// MemorySafetyFuzz.jet the twin of Tools/gauntlet/harness/memory-safety-fuzz.mjs
// (the memory_safety_fuzz axis adapter), Policy.jet that of the
// performance-law exports of Tools/gauntlet/harness/run.mjs (the strict
// performance policy, its issues, peers, metric applicability and ratio
// verdicts), and Shape.jet that of its corpus-entry exports (loading the
// entries and the shape each must have). A program that uses
// it is a `<name>/run.jet` whose leading `package: { … }` block declares
// `jet_gauntlet_kit: <path to Tools/gauntlet/kit>` and imports the names it
// needs with `use jet_gauntlet_kit.[…]`.
name: "jet_gauntlet_kit"
version: "0.0.1"
edition: "2026"
